# The Allen algebra as Academic Meta Tool roles and axioms.
#
# Extracted in step S3 from the Turtle block hard-coded twice in
# de.rgzm.alligator.functions.AMTEvents (PRIMER A8, D-11). Both copies in that
# file are identical and both agree, triple for triple, with the block in the
# published reference outputs -- except for two corrections made in step S6b,
# once running the file through AMT.engine had shown what they do:
#
# 1. RCA0105, RCA0119 and RCA0133 carried the inverse role where composing
#    with `equals` must yield the identity, so `s o e` now gives `s`, `d o e`
#    gives `d` and `f o e` gives `f` (PRIMER D-20);
# 2. SDA001 and SDA002 declared `q` and `e` self-disjoint, forbidding what the
#    same file derives, and are gone (PRIMER D-19).
#
# The general AMT vocabulary that precedes this block in the Java source is
# deliberately not carried over: `amt:Concept rdfs:subClassOf rdfs:Class` and
# the twelve triples with it belong to AMT.engine, which loads its own
# ontology/amt.ttl (PRIMER A4).
#
# The layout below -- section comments, one triple per line, single-quoted
# labels -- is the published one and is kept as it stands, so that a diff
# against any existing AMT file stays readable. rdflib reads it, nothing
# rewrites it.
#
# Origin: https://github.com/leiza-rse/alligator, MIT, LEIZA.


# Concepts
rgzm:Event rdf:type amt:Concept .
rgzm:Event rdfs:label 'Event' .
rgzm:Event amt:placeholder 'name of event' .

